Subject: [PATCH 3/3] gguf-py: Q2_0 block size is 30 bytes

GGMLQuantizationType.Q2_0 was registered as (64, 2 + 16), the old
18-byte block. The current Q2_0 block is 30 bytes: fp16 d (2), 4 bytes
of 4-bit sub-block scales, 16 bytes of low bits and 8 bytes of high bits
for 64 weights. gguf-py derives tensor byte sizes from this table, so
reading or writing Q2_0 tensors would mis-size them. Use
(64, 2 + 4 + 16 + 8).

Checked by reading the table against block_q2_0 in ggml-common.h
(sizeof == 30, static_assert). Not run: numpy is not available in the
test environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gguf-py/gguf/constants.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py b/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py
index 8d0cad5..8688705 100644
--- a/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py
+++ b/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py
@@ -5227,7 +5227,7 @@ GGML_QUANT_SIZES: dict[GGMLQuantizationType, tuple[int, int]] = {
     GGMLQuantizationType.MXFP4:   (32, 1 + 16),
     GGMLQuantizationType.NVFP4:   (64, 4 + 32),
     GGMLQuantizationType.Q1_0:    (128, 2 + 16),
-    GGMLQuantizationType.Q2_0:    (64, 2 + 16),
+    GGMLQuantizationType.Q2_0:    (64, 2 + 4 + 16 + 8),
 }
 
 
